WEBVTT

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.190
Whoa, look!

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.730
Ain’t that Volg Zangief?

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.280
He came back to Japan?

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.660
Yeah, color me surprised.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.280
He’s still in top form despite his absence.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.130
Hello there. It’s nice to meet you all.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.790
U-Uh, yeah.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.000
Nice to meet you.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.260
You’re free to use any of our equipment.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.750
I’ll introduce you to someone in America whom I know and trust once I get a hold of him.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.890
Until then, you can do your workout here.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.990
Thank you very much!

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.030
Let’s ask Volg tomorrow!

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.990
There’s no better sparring partner for the Sawamura fight!

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:00.920
He’s got both the technical skills and the guts! He’d be perfect!

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.930
I’m against it.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.970
I know I shouldn’t say it, but he’s not one of us.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.590
The only ones who should help Senpai are those closest to him.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.950
Well, he has a good point.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.630
Leave your feelings out of this!

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:18.480
You want Ippo to win, don’t you?

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.120
Those two are really intense.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.090
<i>He’s still going?</i>

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.960
<i>I guess a one-time quitter like me is nothing like an active boxer.</i>

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.320
You know we’re right, Itagaki!

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.230
Think about Ippo.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.360
H-Hi there!

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.560
What’re you doing, Volg?

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.740
I’m polishing it. They told me to make it nice and shiny.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.220
Nice and shiny?

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.720
Who said that?

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:10.970
Team Aoki!

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:13.750
They’re gone!

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.030
Hey! What are you making our guest do?

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.750
W-We thought he was a new member!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:24.130
You dipsticks! He fought Makunouchi-
senpai in a very close match!

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.840
Where’s your respect for him?

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.850
Come on, you know there’s no ill will.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.910
That’s not the point here!

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.500
So we <i>should</i>  respect him?

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:42.400
H-Here.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.760
It’s how to beat the Dempsey Roll.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:51.370
Senpai... is now in your hands.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.890
Do it as a favor to us too.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.620
Can you please take him on?

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.180
I realized only a short while ago

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.660
that I’m not nearly as conditioned as I was before I retired.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.640
I’m not even sure if I can last a single round.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.330
Then all you have to do is one round!

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.640
Will that do Makunouchi any good?

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.800
You’re the only one who can do it!

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.530
Please, just think it over.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.630
<i>Makunouchi is very tough.</i>

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.930
<i>I won’t be of any use to him.</i>

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:35.850
<i>Still...</i>

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.540
<i>His friends are very worried about him.</i>

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.170
<i>Makunouchi is also very anxious.</i>

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.130
<i>But why?</i>

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.180
<i>Sawamura.</i>

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.490
<i>Is he the one making Makunouchi so terrified?</i>

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.380
I’m home!

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.870
I’m back too!

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.160
Good job today!

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:17.850
Huh?

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:33.870
<i>Sawamura.</i>

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:38.680
<i>Not only does he scare Makunouchi...</i>

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.670
<i>Makunouchi can’t possibly beat him.</i>

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:43.690
<i>I just need</i>

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.610
<i>enough stamina to last three rounds.</i>

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.810
<i>I’ll put into practice what’s written here.</i>

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.020
<i>The Sawamura Scenario...</i>

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.330
<i>is undoubtedly something straight from hell.</i>

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.530
<i>The Dempsey Roll is useless against him.</i>

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.810
<i>Makunouchi will be buried along with that move.</i>

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:04.160
<i>If that’s the case...</i>

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.220
<i>Then  </i>I...

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.590
<i>will bury him!</i>

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.060
Volg’s about to leave?

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.060
Yeah.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.090
He’s found someone in America.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.860
He’ll be with my coach’s friend, Hama Dankichi-san.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:32.450
Since he’s a world-class trainer, Volg-san must be psyched.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.530
He’s been training day and night for the past week.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.440
It’s almost as if he's got a fight coming up.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:00.180
Volg-san!

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.410
Ma’am!

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:06.120
I’ve finished making supper, so I came to get you.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.170
Thank you very much.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:11.830
Ippo told me that you’re going to America.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.910
Thanks for taking care of me for all this time.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.080
Will you be okay by yourself in America?

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.850
Can you speak English?

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:21.700
I’ll be fine.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:27.170
I owe Makunouchi and his coach a huge debt of gratitude.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.710
They found an American contact for me very quickly.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.930
Really? Good luck, Volg-san.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:36.530
Now let’s go home and have dinner.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:37.620
Of course!

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.210
Let’s go, Wanpo.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.730
You’ll miss him too, right, Wanpo?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:44.730
<i>Yes.</i>

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.360
<i>I must leave this place quickly.</i>

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.070
<i>This place is simply too warm and welcoming.</i>

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.860
Oh, there you are!

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:58.130
You came to get him too?

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:01.190
Umezawa-kun said he’s about to starve to death.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.830
That’s not good!

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.270
We're running home!

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:06.620
You’re not beating me!

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.500
<i>I’ve been training for a whole week!</i>

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.380
<i>I guess I’m still not conditioned.</i>

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.760
<i>But time’s running out.</i>

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:17.380
<i>I have to do it.</i>

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.720
<i>I must thank you by showing you the Sawamura Scenario.</i>

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.250
I won!

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.960
I have a favor to ask... Makunouchi.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.410
A favor? What can I do?

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.910
Volg-san...

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.380
I was wondering why they called us here so damn early in the morning.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:19.400
So Volg asked him to be his sparring partner, eh?

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.930
Will he beat the Dempsey?

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:25.100
His flight for America is scheduled for today.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.910
So this is his goodbye gift?

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:31.380
<i>He wouldn’t be out for blood if that were so.</i>

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.440
<i>It looks like he finally got back</i>

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.000
<i>the desire to challenge the strong, just like a real boxer.</i>

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.140
You may begin.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.070
H-He’s fast!

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.780
The White Fang?!

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.160
Whoa! Is he fighting for real?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.870
A Gazelle Punch!

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.590
Ippo’s also dead serious!

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.830
<i>The third round.</i>

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:43.910
<i>Indeed...</i>

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:49.810
<i>Indeed, he’s able to go on longer than me.</i>

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.370
<i>I can’t withstand his punches anymore.</i>

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.050
<i>Volg-san...</i>

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.610
<i>He’s swinging from one blind spot to another.</i>

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.990
<i>And he’s using those recoils to aid his hard punches.</i>

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:25.610
<i>I-Is this the Dempsey Roll?</i>

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.370
I-Is he going to beat it?

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.250
You know he can’t!

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.080
He’s too worn out to make it happen!

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:37.810
His guard!

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.670
Shit! He’s wide open!

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.520
Don’t do it, Ippo!

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.130
<i>He’s in a blind spot.</i>

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.050
<i>Now!</i>

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.810
<i>There you are!</i>

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:56.560
<i>I can see your right hook, Makunouchi!</i>

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:00.690
<i>The kid can't stop the momentum of his recoil!</i>

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.570
<i>This is the...</i>

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.570
<i>Sawamura Scenario!</i>

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:33.010
Ippo!

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:34.570
Crap! He’s foaming at the mouth!

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:35.270
Senpai!

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.720
Don’t move him! Get a wet towel!

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:49.490
He can’t ask for a better parting gift. We thank you.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:55.500
Makunouchi, I know you will come back from this.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:12:00.040
It ain’t easy making your way up in America, so prepare yourself.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:02.670
I’ll speak for Ippo and thank you.

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:03.870
Thanks very much!

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.000
Kick ass!

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:09.170
I’ll be back.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:18.980
Ma’am, thanks for everything you did for me.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.170
Take these with you.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:25.820
They’re charms for a safe trip, good health, and constant victories.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:28.760
Here.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:36.780
Can you do me one last favor?

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.250
Sure, anything you ask.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:44.710
Can you say, “udachi tebe, synok”?

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.150
Wh-What’s that?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.630
That sure is an odd request.

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:53.140
<i>Udachi tebe, synok.</i>

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.550
Did I do it right?

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.060
Volg-san?

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:04.220
<i>Spasibo... mat.</i>

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:08.150
Oh yeah,

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.290
what did those words mean, anyway?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.210
That’s Russian, right?

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:17.250
Yeah... they’re some magic words you say in Japan to feel better.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.410
Really?

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:23.870
<i>Udachi tebe, synok.</i>

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.240
<i>Spasibo, mat</i>

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.330
Too bad Ippo couldn’t see you off.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:42.730
It’s fine. He saw me off the last time I left anyway.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:43.770
But...

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:47.900
There's no need for goodbyes this time.

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:50.900
Even if we’re an ocean apart, I know we’ll meet again.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:57.310
As long as we’re both still boxing, I know it.

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:00.580
I’ll make sure Ippo hears that!

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:19.140
That must have been devastating.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:23.680
It went so far beyond reckoning
 that even I was surprised.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.690
So the Dempsey Roll is dead, huh.

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:31.360
Yeah, but there’s one more thing.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:34.070
Something even more shocking.

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:36.070
What’s that?

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:40.270
That counter gives back twice the destructive power as the Dempsey.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.950
Volg was very much aware of that.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:48.080
Volg was kind enough to just match up the timing with the punch.

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:50.590
H-He just matched them up?

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:53.830
He went easy on you.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.840
You were knocked out cold by a mercy punch.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:02.730
You know Sawamura will not be that merciful.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.930
He will punch using his full strength.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.600
Then what’ll happen to you?

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.550
If your move is the only thing he'll do in,

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:14.760
then all you have to do is regain 
consciousness and start all over again.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.860
But what if the very unthinkable happens?

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:22.410
What if you never regain consciousness again?

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:29.860
Is Senpai still on the roof?

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.250
That must’ve been a real blow.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:35.760
He found out exactly how he’s going to lose.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:41.540
It might have been better if he’d never known.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:46.230
Who’d wanna fight a match knowing <i>that’s</i>  waiting for him?

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.770
But he can’t back out now.

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:50.770
Of course he won’t!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.320
Senpai won’t let it end like this!

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:57.530
Volg-san even sparred with him hoping he’ll rise to the occasion!

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:59.250
Well...

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.240
You have a point.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:03.560
Will he stand the pressure, though?

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.290
It’s a lot, even for him.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:08.640
That was a very sobering parting gift from Volg.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:13.960
Kid?

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:16.870
I’ll do everything I can do!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:21.720
Whatever doubts I have, I'll try to erase some of them with all the training I can think of!

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:25.890
If I do that, I’ll fill myself with renewed hope!

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:29.390
You’ll find hope in <i>this</i>  situation?

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:30.910
Yes!

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:36.150
Now that I know how he’ll beat me, it should be easy to come up with a counterstrategy!

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:42.780
If that’s not true, then Volg-san
 did all that work for nothing.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:43.580
That’s right!

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:50.160
<i>He’s just bluffing, trying to maintain his empty bravado.</i>

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:56.060
<i>But if he didn’t, he would be completely consumed by crippling fear.</i>

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.450
<i>There  </i>is <i>a way.</i>

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.170
<i>But...</i>

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:02.250
<i>I’m not telling him.</i>

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:06.870
<i>That would make those tough
 legs of his scream out in pain.</i>

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:10.730
<i>He’ll need to go past the movable limits of normal human joints.</i>

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:14.820
<i>That punch will take years off his life as a boxer.</i>

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:18.980
<i>I’m not sure if I should tell him that secret later on in his career.</i>

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:21.850
<i>This is certainly no time to waver.</i>

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:25.170
<i>But that’s not an easy decision to make.</i>

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:31.000
You must be feeling lonely

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:33.620
now that Volg ain’t around.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:34.380
Yeah.

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:37.160
You’d have liked the look he sported when he left.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.980
He looked like a real winner.

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:42.380
He even said he’ll come back to see you.

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.260
Probably when you're both world champions.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:47.430
World champions?

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:50.570
Maybe in America. It’s not an
 easy thing to achieve here.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:53.920
It’s just a matter of time as long as you both keep winning.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:57.410
So you better win your next title defense, you hear?

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:00.240
I want to win.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.820
I want to win, but...

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.410
<i>I still don’t see that happening.</i>

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:09.410
<i>I might not even have a ghost of a chance.</i>

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:21.590
<i>No matter how much I run, I’m still anxious.</i>

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:23.800
<i>I'm only thinking of the negatives!</i>

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:31.020
<i>I’ve been pulling these tires for quite a while now.</i>

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:35.770
<i>I know I need to build up my legs.</i>

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.440
<i>But how is that the key?</i>

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:42.070
<i>Stop doubting!</i>

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:45.950
<i>The coach always makes you do these things for a reason!</i>

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:47.910
<i>But...</i>

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:52.330
<i>He knocked me out cold with just one punch.</i>

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:55.870
<i>Will every counterpuncher use that move?</i>

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.340
<i>All they need to do is get the rhythm down.</i>

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.880
<i>My rhythm is easy to gauge.</i>

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:06.880
<i>Then that rhythm...</i>

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.810
<i>needs to change!</i>

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:34.310
<i>The recoil was so great that a sudden stop puts too much load on my hips and knees.</i>

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:35.580
<i>But...</i>

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:37.960
<i>This is it!</i>

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:40.790
<i>I’m sure this is exactly what my coach wanted me to do!</i>

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:45.090
<i>If I can build up my legs to withstand that force...</i>

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.840
<i>That pathetic little move will be utterly pulverized.</i>

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:53.570
<i>Tell me if it’s really pathetic during our fight.</i>

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:54.430
<i>There...</i>

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:59.540
<i>Sawamura-san will see a Dempsey Roll that’s a little bit different!</i>

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:04.070
<i>I can see how the Dempsey Roll will evolve!</i>
